From e375576e7eb7a4af3dfa1c697476128e4a03f4a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anders Madsen <madsenanders97@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:24:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] laguna: 0129 add always-on XNU msgbuf mirroring and RAM-dump
 stages

R4 panic-capture/logdump lane, host only. Add XNU-MSGBUF v1 at pmsg+0x40000: a 64-byte header plus a reserved 1 MiB ring, active in live msg_size geometry. Initialize immediately after arm_vm_init before serial_init with the existing single 4 MiB Device ml_io_map, replay the static msgbuf, then append every kernel msgbuf byte from log_putc_locked only when mbp==msgbufp. Data precedes total/tail metadata; appends alone own stream fields so periodic flushes cannot tear write/total pairs. OSLOG resize rebases/replays, a one-second thread refreshes source metadata/seq, both panic rungs flush before capture dedup, and halt/reboot flushes use the 0124 nofault discipline while retaining last-valid metadata.

Add independent R3-compatible breadcrumbs: compact 12-u32 stages at pmsg+0x1050 (cleared exactly per boot, preserving M1/boot/DIAG) plus the frozen CRC/DONE LGLW slots at +0x1100/+0x1180. start.s writes gated XNU_ENTRY physically before MMU using the normal marker handoff; root/install, launchd attempt, image activation, shared-region, XNU init and panic use the published stage/detail ABI. lagunalogdump=1 defaults ON; =0 disables only these additions, leaving 0123/0124 PAN1/console capture independent.

Validation: isolated DEVELOPMENT_ARM64_LAGUNA builds have zero compile errors. QEMU default: legacy 20/20, new mirror 12/12, exact live msgbuf tail equality, seq 3->9 with PANIC|EARLY_REPLAY, R2 accepted PANIC. Opt-out: legacy 20/20 and mirror/stage absence 5/5. Host selftests 11/11, R2 57/57, pmsg contract PASS on all three DTBs, marker stub structural verification PASS.
